accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final  type  surgical pathology  pathology report  removed_accession_id  breast mastectomy   partial or simple  accessioned on  removed_date  lester  susan  m d  ph d   diagnosis  by lester susan m d  ph d   left breast  wire localized excision for a lobulated mass and a clip marking a  prior core needle biopsy   severely atypical ductal hyperplasia involving a sclerosing papilloma   block 10  levels examined   see note   an immunohistochemical study for  p63 reveals basally located myoepithelial cells throughout the lesion  as  well as scattered cells within the areas of hyperplasia  the entire  sclerosing papilloma measures 0 8cm in size   the closest margin is lateral which is   0 1cm from the sclerosing  papilloma   the prior core needle biopsy site is present associated with the  sclerosing papilloma   note  this lesion is evaluated in conjunction with the prior core needle  biopsy  bwh consultation  removed_accession_id   and both show similar features   the hyperplasia is difficult to evaluate due to the involvement of the  papilloma  areas of the hyperplasia demonstrate regular cribriform  spaces  some of the spaces are filled with mucin or basement membrane  material  suggestive of mucinous and collagenous spherulosis  this is  supported by the p63 study which suggests that the epithelial  proliferation is made up of both luminal and myoepithelial cells   however  other spaces appear empty  more typical of dcis   the differential diagnosis includes a low grade dcis versus adh involving  a papilloma  the latter diagnosis is favored due to the lack of  definitive areas of dcis outside the area of this focal lesion  however   the lesion is very close to the margin  re excision may be helpful to  exclude an adjacent area of dcis   dr  james connolly reviewed selected slides and concurs with the  interpretation of this lesion as severely atypical ductal hyperplasia   clinical data   history  status post cor